diagnostic_evidence.quote:
Without loss of generality, the following noise model is adopted
\begin{equation}\label{eqn:noise}
\Lambda_n=\Lambda_{\sigma_D}-\Lambda_{\sigma_{bg}}+N,
\end{equation}
where $N$ is a bounded operator.

failure_location.quote:
Let $\Lambda_n$, $N$ as defined in~\eqref{eqn:noise}, with $\delta=\norm{N}_2$. Let $\lambda_k$, $\tilde{\lambda}_k$ the eigenvalues of $\Lambda_{\sigma_D}-\Lambda_{\sigma_{bg}}$ and $\Lambda_n$, respectively, ordered in a decreasing order. Then
    \begin{equation*}
        \lvert \tilde{\lambda}_k - \lambda_k \rvert \leq \delta
    \end{equation*}
